+# Privacy by design notes
+
+## Data minimization
+- The site collects no personal data: no cookies, no scripts, no analytics, no forms, no storage.
+- The server does not log requests (no IPs or URLs are persisted).
+- `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer` and `<meta name="referrer">` prevent URLs leaking to other sites.
+- `Permissions-Policy` disables camera, microphone, geolocation, payment and FLoC/Topics.
+
+## Third-party audit
+| Resource | Previously | Now |
+|---|---|---|
+| Hero image (images.unsplash.com) | Fetched from Unsplash on every visit, exposing visitor IP/UA to a third party | Self-hosted at `/assets/hero.jpg` |
+
+No third-party requests remain. The CSP (`default-src 'none'`, only `'self'` for styles/images) enforces this:
+adding any external resource is blocked by browsers, forcing a deliberate review.
+Re-audit whenever a dependency, embed, font, or script is added.
+
+## Secure data handling
+- HTTPS only: HSTS and `upgrade-insecure-requests` (serve behind TLS; HSTS is ignored over plain HTTP).
+- The static server only allows GET/HEAD, rejects path traversal and null bytes, and serves only `public/`.
+- Inline styles were moved to `public/styles.css`, so the CSP needs no `unsafe-inline`.
+- Any future feature collecting data (accounts, orders, rewards) must collect only what is needed, state its purpose
+  in `/privacy-policy`, use `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax` cookies, and avoid third-party trackers.
+
+## Security headers (see `server.js`)
+CSP, HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, COOP/COEP/CORP,
+X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies. Deploying behind a CDN/proxy requires replicating these headers.
